2. User-Friendly Navigation: Easy-to-use navigation is vital for retaining visitors. Studies show that 94% of consumers consider easy navigation the most important website feature. 
WEB.COM

3. Search Engine Optimization (SEO): Optimizing websites for search engines helps improve visibility and attract potential customers. This includes keyword research, on-page optimization, and building quality backlinks. 
EN.WIKIPEDIA.ORG

4. Visual Design Elements: Incorporating appealing visuals like images, colors, and videos can significantly impact user engagement. For instance, 40% of consumers value images, 39% value color, and 21% value video on company websites. 
BLOG.HUBSPOT.COM

5. Website Performance and Loading Speed: Fast-loading websites enhance user experience and are favored by search engines. Optimizing site speed can lead to higher user satisfaction and improved search rankings.

6. Mobile Optimization: With the increasing use of mobile devices, ensuring websites are mobile-friendly is essential. Google's "Mobilegeddon" update in 2015 emphasized the importance of mobile-friendly sites for search rankings.

7. Conversion Rate Optimization (CRO): Designing websites to guide visitors toward desired actions, such as making a purchase or signing up for a newsletter, is crucial for business success.

8. Web Accessibility: Making websites accessible to all users, including those with disabilities, is both ethical and beneficial for reaching a broader audience. This involves adhering to accessibility standards and guidelines.

By focusing on these areas, small businesses can create effective websites that attract and retain customers, ultimately contributing to their growth and success.